<title>USA: Motivepower says to cut $1m in annual costs.</title>
<headline>Motivepower says to cut $1m in annual costs.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>MotivePower Industries Inc said in order to support its rapid international expansion it is taking cost-cutting measures to save the company approximately $1 million a year.</p>
<p>The company said it may reduce its work force by about 40 employees because it will vacate two leased facilities in Pittsburgh by year-end. These facilities are redundant, MotivePower said.</p>
<p>The company plans to modernize and consolidate these operations into its Braddock, Pa., facilities. As a result, the company will also relocate its traction motor gear and pinion manufacturing operations from Braddock.</p>
<p>Motor Coils employs 385 people in the Pittsburgh area, 200 in Emporium, Pa., and 50 in St. Louis for a total of 635 employees.</p>
</text>
